 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The only `restrict*` declarations in the diff are `restrict_apply`, `iteratedFDeriv_extend_restrict`, `iteratedFDeriv_restrict_apply`, `norm_restrict_le`, `restrictL_apply`, `norm_restrictL_le_one`, `restrict_self` and `restrict_restrict`. The `extend` and `iteratedFDeriv*` accessors in the same file do get `_zero`/`_add`/`_smul` lemmas.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Holder/Domain.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] restrict_zero`, `restrict_add (f g) : (f + g).restrict h = f.restrict h + g.restrict h` and `restrict_smul (c f) : (c \u2022 f).restrict h = c \u2022 f.restrict h`, each proved by `ext x; simp`, and build `restrictL` from them.",
   "issue": "`restrict` has no simp lemmas for zero, `+` or `\u2022`. A term like `(f + g).restrict h` cannot be simplified unless the user first rewrites it as `restrictL h (f + g)`. The PR proves these facts only inside the anonymous `map_add'`/`map_smul'` fields of `restrictL`.",
   "line": 690
  }
 ],
